WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.127
- [Robin] Welcome to
Tasty's nacho cook-Off.

00:00:02.127 --> 00:00:03.944
Three members of the Tasty team face off

00:00:03.944 --> 00:00:06.591
to see who can make the best nachos.

00:00:06.591 --> 00:00:08.524
Competing in this event
are Robin Broadfoot,

00:00:08.524 --> 00:00:09.692
Tasty video producer,

00:00:09.692 --> 00:00:11.489
Hannah Williams, Tasty video producer,

00:00:11.489 --> 00:00:14.442
and Nick Guillory, Tasty
social media strategist.

00:00:14.442 --> 00:00:16.687
(upbeat surfer music)

00:00:16.687 --> 00:00:19.463
So today I'm making
steak and potato nachos,

00:00:19.463 --> 00:00:22.484
so I made this into a
video and once it was made,

00:00:22.484 --> 00:00:24.208
I usually like to take my food home,

00:00:24.208 --> 00:00:26.089
but in this case, it didn't happen,

00:00:26.089 --> 00:00:27.848
because all my coworkers ate it.

00:00:27.848 --> 00:00:29.925
I've got three russet potatoes,
which I'm going to season

00:00:29.925 --> 00:00:32.533
with olive oil, salt, pepper and paprika.

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:36.306
I'll bake the potatoes at 450
degrees for about 20 minutes.

00:00:36.306 --> 00:00:38.906
While that's cooking, I'm
going to season the steak and

00:00:38.906 --> 00:00:42.006
get a nice sear on them roughly
three minutes each side.

00:00:42.006 --> 00:00:43.221
I'll flip the steak once.

00:00:43.221 --> 00:00:46.077
After that, I'll let the steak
rest for eight to 10 minutes

00:00:46.077 --> 00:00:48.306
because it's still cooking after
you take it out of the pan.

00:00:48.306 --> 00:00:50.323
Once the potatoes are
ready, I'm going to lay them

00:00:50.323 --> 00:00:52.573
around the cast iron pan and
sprinkle the steak on them.

00:00:52.573 --> 00:00:54.759
When everything's assembled,
I'm gonna cover the dish

00:00:54.759 --> 00:00:57.438
with freshly grated cheddar
and Monterey Jack cheese.

00:00:57.438 --> 00:00:59.580
And then I'm just gonna
boil it seven to 10 minutes

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.443
until everything's nice and
melted and then top it off

00:01:01.443 --> 00:01:03.263
with sour cream and salsa and serve it.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.368
When I was younger, I wasn't
really allowed in the kitchen.

00:01:05.368 --> 00:01:07.168
My mom would always shoo me away,

00:01:07.168 --> 00:01:09.170
but then going to college,
my dad said this would be

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.197
a good way to go on dates,
if women knew you could cook.

00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:15.353
- [Hannah] Today I'm making
Korean pork belly nachos.

00:01:15.353 --> 00:01:17.166
I make a lot of desserts for Tasty.

00:01:17.166 --> 00:01:19.110
I'm kind of known for making cheesecake.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.983
This is a little out of my comfort zone.

00:01:21.983 --> 00:01:22.816
So the first thing I'm gonna do

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:24.496
is get this pork in the marinade.

00:01:24.496 --> 00:01:27.617
It's gonna marinate in some
kimchi juice, soy sauce,

00:01:27.617 --> 00:01:30.194
sesame oil, Korean red pepper, and honey.

00:01:30.194 --> 00:01:32.839
Then I'm gonna sear it on
extremely high heat to try to

00:01:32.839 --> 00:01:35.993
render the fat a little bit
to get it nice and crispy.

00:01:35.993 --> 00:01:37.963
And while that cooks, I'm
gonna dice my toppings.

00:01:37.963 --> 00:01:41.185
I got some red onions, some
kimchi, and I'll layer that

00:01:41.185 --> 00:01:43.083
on top of the pork and the chips.

00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:45.573
I'm gonna grate some
cheddar and Monterey Jack

00:01:45.573 --> 00:01:48.394
and let that melt on top of the nachos.

00:01:48.394 --> 00:01:49.470
And then my finishing touches

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.475
are gonna be some diced
tomatoes and green onions

00:01:52.475 --> 00:01:55.650
and that's gonna go on top of
everything once it's melted.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:58.031
And I'm gonna mix some sour
cream with kimchi juice

00:01:58.031 --> 00:02:00.594
and drizzle that on top
as a finishing touch

00:02:00.594 --> 00:02:01.883
to tie it all together.

00:02:01.883 --> 00:02:04.264
When I think of nachos, I
think of kind of the standard

00:02:04.264 --> 00:02:07.649
salsa, beans, cheese,
whatever you like on that,

00:02:07.649 --> 00:02:10.145
so this is just a really,
really different type of nacho.

00:02:10.145 --> 00:02:13.307
It's not too loaded, it's not too heavy,

00:02:13.307 --> 00:02:15.103
but it still has a lot of flavor.

00:02:15.103 --> 00:02:16.761
- [Nick] Hi, I'm Nick and I'm making

00:02:16.761 --> 00:02:20.116
spicy, cheesy, blackened
chicken nachos today.

00:02:20.116 --> 00:02:22.461
These guys cook like this all the time.

00:02:22.461 --> 00:02:25.309
This is my first time like
cooking with all these cameras

00:02:25.309 --> 00:02:28.081
and these fancy lights
and these microphones.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.053
Like I'm not gonna lie, I'm scared.

00:02:30.053 --> 00:02:32.776
I'm gonna season my chicken
with cajun seasoning,

00:02:32.776 --> 00:02:34.822
garlic powder, chili
powder, and hot sauce.

00:02:34.822 --> 00:02:37.186
While that's cooking, I'm
going to cut up some onions,

00:02:37.186 --> 00:02:39.260
tomatoes, jalapenos, and corn.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:42.389
I'll saute those veggies
with more cajun seasoning.

00:02:42.389 --> 00:02:44.461
I'll add the blackened
chicken to the mixture

00:02:44.461 --> 00:02:46.470
and top it all off with freshly grated

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.920
pepper jack cheese and salsa.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.922
Broil that until the cheese is melted.

00:02:50.922 --> 00:02:54.237
I'm from Louisiana and I love spicy food.

00:02:54.237 --> 00:02:56.198
I like to entertain at home.

00:02:56.198 --> 00:02:58.085
This will be like a cute little appetizer,

00:02:58.085 --> 00:03:01.454
get everybody nice and
spicy and moving around,

00:03:01.454 --> 00:03:03.988
and hot and sweaty before we go dancing.

00:03:03.988 --> 00:03:07.123
(upbeat surfer music)

00:03:07.123 --> 00:03:08.718
- [Taste-Tester 1] What kind
of beautiful mess is this

00:03:08.718 --> 00:03:09.551
that I walked into?

00:03:09.551 --> 00:03:10.527
- [Taste-Tester 2] That's
exactly what nachos are,

00:03:10.527 --> 00:03:11.944
a beautiful mess.

00:03:14.707 --> 00:03:15.906
- [Taste-Tester 1] This is real crunchy.

00:03:15.906 --> 00:03:16.739
It's got a nice crunch to it.

00:03:16.739 --> 00:03:17.572
- [Taste-Tester 3] Got
a nice crunch to it.

00:03:17.572 --> 00:03:18.858
- [Taste-Tester 2] I
love this, but it doesn't

00:03:18.858 --> 00:03:20.297
have that classic nacho cheese.

00:03:20.297 --> 00:03:21.130
- [Taste-Tester 3] Yeah.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.310
- [Taste-Tester 1] It's
very original though.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:25.175
Okay, let's go to the next one.

00:03:25.175 --> 00:03:27.034
It almost functions kind of like a dip.

00:03:27.034 --> 00:03:30.738
This looks like a little bit
of salsa, a little cheese.

00:03:30.738 --> 00:03:32.107
That is delicious.

00:03:32.107 --> 00:03:33.457
- [Taste-Tester 2] It is spicy, though.

00:03:33.457 --> 00:03:34.290
- [Taste-Tester 1] This is the perfect

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:37.145
ratio of cheese right here.

00:03:37.145 --> 00:03:37.978
Steak!

00:03:37.978 --> 00:03:38.811
- [Taste-Tester 2] Steak and potatoes.

00:03:38.811 --> 00:03:40.089
- [Taste-Tester 1] I want this so badly.

00:03:40.089 --> 00:03:40.966
- [Taste-Tester 2] Are you kidding me?

00:03:40.966 --> 00:03:41.799
- [Taste-Tester 1]
There's a lot of cheese.

00:03:41.799 --> 00:03:42.632
- [Taste-Tester 2] Oh
wait, are there no chips?

00:03:42.632 --> 00:03:44.641
Can we all agree though if this one had

00:03:44.641 --> 00:03:46.371
crispy potato chips, it would win?

00:03:46.371 --> 00:03:47.724
- [Taste-Tester 3] For sure, the flavors

00:03:47.724 --> 00:03:49.487
in this one was on point.

00:03:49.487 --> 00:03:50.320
- [Taste-Tester 1] Mainly
we're just thankful that

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:51.534
they made this food for us.

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:52.367
- [Taste-Tester 3] I can't stop eating.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:53.654
- [Taste-Tester 2] Yeah, I'm
just gonna keep eating it.

00:03:53.654 --> 00:03:57.357
My winner, my decision is this guy.

00:03:57.357 --> 00:03:59.430
- [Taste-Tester 1] Mine
is the blackened chicken.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:02.362
- [Taste-Tester 2] Angela?

00:04:02.362 --> 00:04:05.324
- [Angela] Mine was the
blackened chicken, as well.

00:04:05.324 --> 00:04:09.988
- [Nick] Yeah! I won, I
won, I win everything.

00:04:09.988 --> 00:04:11.754
Yes, what do I win?

00:04:11.754 --> 00:04:14.921
(upbeat surfer music)

00:04:21.248 --> 00:04:22.915
- [Narrator] Oh yes!

